WEBVTT

00:00:56.849 --> 00:01:00.490
of people doing mostly representational art,

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:02.523
that modern art, comparatively speaking,

00:01:02.523 --> 00:01:04.863
is about 15 minutes old,

00:01:04.863 --> 00:01:06.761
yet now pervasive.

00:01:06.761 --> 00:01:08.705
As with many other important innovations,

00:01:08.705 --> 00:01:12.325
those radical ideas required no new technology,

00:01:12.325 --> 00:01:15.218
just fresh thinking and a willingness to experiment,

00:01:15.218 --> 00:01:19.386
plus resiliency in the face of near-universal criticism

00:01:19.386 --> 00:01:20.840
and rejection.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.357
In our home, art was everywhere.

00:01:23.357 --> 00:01:24.928
It was like oxygen,

00:01:24.928 --> 00:01:28.090
around us and necessary for life.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:29.949
As I watched him paint,

00:01:29.949 --> 00:01:32.256
Dad taught me that art